iatives including  amendments to the trust indenture Act a  variety of accounting issues including  opinion shopping mandatory peer review  and the recommendation of the National  Commission on fraudulent financial  reporting proxy regulations and mutual  fund advertising all these issues are  significant fortunately the current  commissioners and the Commission staff  possess the high levels of knowledge  competence and judgment necessary to  address dress this agenda I considered a  privilege to serve on this commission at  this time and to have an opportunity to  help develop with the other  commissioners the staff and the Congress  the overall regulatory approach that  will best serve our nation's interest  lots of question your regulatory cousin  the commodity futures trader Trading  Commission said that their preliminary  data showed little index trading during  the week of October 19 another  questioner says the CFTC has reported  that index arbitrage contributed to only  nine percent of New York Stock Exchange  sell orders during the market crash so  are you using is the SEC using a  different set of numbers what accounts  for this the Securities Exchange  Commission is cooperating with the CFTC  and the gathering of data we are not yet  complete in our data gathering process  and neither is the CFTC as I understand  their report we we have found that  during the morning of October 19th there  was significant index arbitrage trading  and that during the day on october  twenty there was significant portfolio  insurance selling i use the word  significant because it is a weasel word  it's a word that does not commit me to  fight indicating what our conclusions  will be we are studying the question  carefully and at this point I can  neither agree nor disagree with the  CFTC's conclusion  we're little investors protected on  Black Monday in other words did they get  a fair shake the question of the  protection of small investors on Black  Monday and indeed during the week of  October 19th is one that we are  concerned with we we know that in many  cases the small investors were not able  to reach their brokers that in many  cases the small investors were not able  to reach their mutual funds and we are  concerned in addition with some order  reading order routing and the execution  problems with regard to small investor  orders we whether or not it's a matter  of unfairness is of course a judgmental  question we had extremely unusual volume  on on Monday and Tuesday of the  nineteenth and twentieth 600 million  shares was roughly twice as much trading  as has ever occurred on the New York  Stock Exchange and in the various  markets so that the breakdown of these  systems I think could have been expected  to even a greater degree than it did  occur and we we will be of course  looking to see whether there was any  deliberate activity on on the part of  brokers to to put the small investors at  the back of the line my tentative guess  is that we were looking primarily at  some systems breakdowns which happen to  affect these small investors more  dramatically than the large one  do you support the proxmire darn bill to  repeal glass-steagall my remarks on  glass-steagall this noon indicated that  we are still studying the question of  repeal of glass-steagall I will be  testifying on December third regarding  that repeal I I can repeat again what I  said in my speech that the Securities  and Exchange Commission believes that in  that in an important condition of  glass-steagall repeal is the  establishment of the principle of  functional regulation that is that when  banks engage in securities activities  they must be regulated as in the same  manner as other members of the  securities industry and we will be  seeking appropriate legislation to to  ensure that result number of variations  on a question which is in this case to  better keep up with the growing  interrelationship among Securities and  future markets that you 