re on  the on the morning of october twenty  seconds the the futures of Standard &amp;  Poor's 500 futures index was an opening  was at a an extremely extreme discount  numbers I think that we're extremely  unusual i think it was sixty 60 points  down from from where it had that hike  that's that was as as large as one could  ever have imagined and we we we looked  at that opening and saw that that what  was happening in the securities markets  on the New York Stock Exchange or what  might happen at the new york stock  exchange would be that people looking at  what the futures market seem to be  predicting for price the futures people  will tell you that there's a price  prediction feature move contained in  there in there in there in there index  and that the futures that predicts price  price discovery is the word they use and  one could imagine that that at the in  the market in New York Stock Exchange  that someone trying to figure out where  to open a stock on on New York Stock  Exchange looking at a futures market  which seemed to be down dramatically  would decide that they had to open their  their their products down  in and buy an enormous number our  thought was that if we could allow the  the stock products to be opened without  having the overhand hang or threat of  the psychological factor at least of  this of this large discount appearing on  the on the various screens around the  country that that it might produce a  more orderly opening we we discussed  this with the we discussed this in a  securities and exchange commission  meeting on the afternoon of the 22nd we  were told during that meeting that the  Chicago virtual work Mercantile Exchange  had introduced price limits and we  decided that that that we that we could  postpone the any formal request for the  introduction of a delayed opening on the  on the futures exchange we did consider  it for the reasons that I that I've  indicated but we did delay on that  Friday morning and we found during 